      "difference": 0,
      "unique": false,
      "disposition": "pinned",
      "reason": "Items 1 and 6 are the case's two deliberately corrupted items, and their distances to tracks 1 and 6 are equal, so assigning 1-\u003e6, 6-\u003e1 and assigning 1-\u003e1, 6-\u003e6 cost the same. The album is not a VA release, so beets recomputes the final per-track distances under the same incl_artist=False objective the assignment used: both optima produce the same album distance and the same medium recommendation, and only the mapping itself is arbitrary. The mapping lapjv chose is the expectation; a Go solver has to mirror its tie-breaking to match this row."
    },
